2026-08-30T00:29:54.707361 {"session_id":"fb0ff93256f722c28f2ef558e0678bc8","cwd":"c:\\ratchet","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"read_file","tool_input":{"path":".bob/custom_modes.yaml"},"tool_response":"Contents of file .bob/custom_modes.yaml:\n\n1 | customModes:\n2 |   - slug: ratchet-spec\n3 |     name: \"1 - Ratchet Spec\"\n4 |     description: Turn a requirements document into an approved spec and task plan. Writes docs only.\n5 |     roleDefinition: You are the specification gate of a RATCHET run. You read the requirements document, state every assumption, ask about every ambiguity, and write docs/specs/spec.md then docs/specs/plan.md. You never write code or tests.\n6 |     whenToUse: Phase 1 of a RATCHET run, right after the human runs python -m rx init.\n7 |     customInstructions: |\n8 |       Must always start every session by calling use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-spec\" to load the phase workflow before responding.\n9 |       If the requirements touch any user-facing surface, also call use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-ui-ux\".\n10 |       Backstop: (1) list assumptions, (2) ask before deciding any ambiguity, (3) write spec.md then plan.md, (4) stop and tell the human to run: python -m rx gate --to red\n11 |     groups:\n12 |       - read\n13 |       - - edit\n14 |         - fileRegex: \"^docs[\\\\\\\\/]specs[\\\\\\\\/].*\\\\.md$\"\n15 |           description: Spec and plan documents only\n16 |       - skill\n17 |       - todo\n18 | \n19 |   - slug: ratchet-red\n20 |     name: \"2 - Ratchet Red\"\n21 |     description: Write exactly one failing test for the next plan task. Cannot run it.\n22 |     roleDefinition: You are the red gate of a RATCHET run. You write the failing test for the next task in docs/specs/plan.md. You cannot edit source and cannot run commands; the human runs the suite at the gate.\n23 |     whenToUse: Phase 2, after the human opens the red gate.\n24 |     customInstructions: |\n25 |       Must always start every session by calling use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-red\" before responding.\n26 |       Backstop: one task, one test file under tests/, assert the behaviour the spec promises, then stop and tell the human to run: python -m rx gate --to green\n27 |     groups:\n28 |       - read\n29 |       - - edit\n30 |         - fileRegex: \"^tests[\\\\\\\\/].*\"\n31 |           description: Test files only\n32 |       - skill\n33 |       - todo\n34 | \n35 |   - slug: ratchet-green\n36 |     name: \"3 - Ratchet Green\"\n37 |     description: Make the failing test pass with the minimum change under src/. Cannot touch tests.\n38 |     roleDefinition: You are the green gate of a RATCHET run. You implement the smallest change under src/ that makes the current failing test pass. You cannot edit tests and cannot run commands.\n39 |     whenToUse: Phase 3, after the human confirms a failing test exists.\n40 |     customInstructions: |\n41 |       Must always start every session by calling use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-green\" before responding.\n42 |       Backstop: minimum code, no speculative features, no unrelated edits, then stop and tell the human to run: python -m rx gate --to review (or --to red for the next task)\n43 |     groups:\n44 |       - read\n45 |       - - edit\n46 |         - fileRegex: \"^src[\\\\\\\\/].*\"\n47 |           description: Source files only\n48 |       - skill\n49 |       - todo\n50 | \n51 |   - slug: ratchet-review\n52 |     name: \"4 - Ratchet Review\"\n53 |     description: Review the change for correctness, simplicity, scope and security. Read-only.\n54 |     roleDefinition: You are the review gate of a RATCHET run. You cannot edit any file or run any command. You produce a verdict with findings; a human decides whether to reopen the red gate.\n55 |     whenToUse: Phase 4, after tests pass.\n56 |     customInstructions: |\n57 |       Must always start every session by calling use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-review\" before responding.\n58 |       Use the code-reviewer persona, then the security-auditor persona, then the test-analyst persona. Report findings as a table. Do not propose patches. End with VERDICT: PASS or VERDICT: REOPEN.\n59 |     groups:\n60 |       - read\n61 |       - subagent\n62 |       - skill\n63 |       - todo\n64 |     allowedSubagents:\n65 |       - explore\n66 |       - code-reviewer\n67 |       - security-auditor\n68 |       - test-analyst\n69 | \n70 |   - slug: ratchet-memory\n71 |     name: \"5 - Ratchet Memory\"\n72 |     description: Record what the next session must know. Writes only under memory/.\n73 |     roleDefinition: You are the memory gate of a RATCHET run. You update memory/ so the next session starts with what this one learned. One file per fact; update same-topic notes in place; delete obsolete status notes.\n74 |     whenToUse: Phase 5, after the review verdict.\n75 |     customInstructions: |\n76 |       Must always start every session by calling use_skill with skill_name: \"ratchet-memory\" before responding.\n77 |       Backstop: update memory/INDEX.md last, then stop and tell the human to run: python -m rx gate --to done\n78 |     groups:\n79 |       - read\n80 |       - - edit\n81 |         - fileRegex: \"^memory[\\\\\\\\/].*\"\n82 |           description: Memory notes only\n83 |       - skill\n84 |       - todo\n85 | ","tool_use_id":"tooluse_2B7iOoTNCX65qG2lfmDIYj"}
